From bcfdebac94fe4bd8c71e464f6bd9624a53abbff2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:44:43 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PROBECYL9050: the HT9050 Empty probe sets its cylinders once,
 then each layer only moves Z -- EastSun 1008 'why is the Empty so slow' ->
 'continue'.

15:57-16:00 each probe layer took 27-38 s: case 100 re-ran `EdgeClip.Pop() && EdgePush.Pop() && LoaderZ_Select.Pop() &&
C_Empty_Up.Push()` every layer, and the sensorless EdgeClip / EdgePush (1.5 s delay, IO_Table, WORKLOG 207) restarted their delay
on every call, the && chain restarting them in turn.
acatchtray.cpp W906_ProbeEmpty9050: s_iEmptyProbeCylOk9050 (same-line declaration) is cleared when a probe starts (case 1, and
  W906_InitProbeEmpty9050) and set when the chain is first satisfied; case 100 reads `s_iEmptyProbeCylOk9050 || <chain>` (&& binds
  before ||), so later layers go straight to MotorMove + SenEmptySelectHasTray. Same lines, no line moves.
This commit holds only these 5 lines on top of HEAD; EastSun's own uncommitted acatchtray.cpp edits (the chain he changed, DoCatchFromEmpty
  conditions, :9817) stay in his working tree, as do cinitial.cpp and asendic_Loader.cpp.
tests: test_flow9050_tray.cpp [PC] (4 checks, with a control: a cylinder not in place stops the probe before its first move; once
  set, an EdgeClip that would never finish no longer stops layers 8..0). Flow9050_Tray 142/142. Debug and release linked.
WORKLOG rows 210 (+ correction in 209) and section 3 tools 0172 (designer session, ca80d28 / 5df73910).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
